<type>(<scope>): <subject>

# Type must be one of:
# feat: A new feature or enhancement.
# fix: A bug fix.
# docs: Documentation changes only.
# style: Formatting, missing semicolons, whitespace, etc.
# refactor: Code changes that neither fix a bug nor add a feature.
# test: Adding or correcting tests.
# chore: Routine tasks, updating build scripts, package managers, etc.
# Subject line must be 50 characters max.

# Body:
# Explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW. Wrap at 72 characters.
# Separate paragraphs with a blank line.

# Footer:
# BREAKING CHANGE: <explanation>
# Closes #<issue-number>

# EXAMPLE:
#   feat(api): Implement secure password hashing with Argon2
#
#   This change updates all user authentication routes to use the modern
#   Argon2 hashing algorithm instead of the legacy bcrypt implementation.
#
#   Argon2 provides superior resistance against brute-force and side-channel
#   attacks, improving the overall security posture of the application.
#   This required updating the `User` model's pre-save hook and adding the
#   new hashing library to dependencies.
# 
#   Closes #148 
